# Restore the WiFi STA configuration wiped by a flash.
# Sequence per CLAUDE.md: power on -> ENAbled 0 -> set fields -> ENAbled 1
# -> APPLY (all-caps; APPL is -113) -> settle -> ADDRess? -> SAVE.
# NETType 1 = STA, SECurity 3 = WPA with passphrase.
#
# VERIFY SYNTAX IS A *LEADING* '?' (batch.sh:33). This file previously used the
# old 'CMD? expected' form, which batch.sh now sends WHOLE as a parameterised
# query -- 'SYSTem:POWer:STATe? 1' returned -108 and aborted the restore at
# line 7 on 2026-10-14. A trailing '?' is part of the mnemonic, never a verify.
#
# AND THE SAVE WAS MISSING: this file's own header described 'settle -> verify
# -> SAVE' while the body stopped at APPLY, so nothing persisted and a reboot
# reverted the restore. Header documented a sequence the body did not implement.
SYSTem:POWer:STATe 1
?SYSTem:POWer:STATe? 1
SYSTem:COMMunicate:LAN:ENAbled 0
SYSTem:COMMunicate:LAN:NETType 1
?SYSTem:COMMunicate:LAN:NETType? 1
SYSTem:COMMunicate:LAN:SECurity 3
?SYSTem:COMMunicate:LAN:SECurity? 3
SYSTem:COMMunicate:LAN:SSID "${WIFI_SSID}"
SYSTem:COMMunicate:LAN:PASs "${WIFI_PASS}"
SYSTem:COMMunicate:LAN:ENAbled 1
?SYSTem:COMMunicate:LAN:ENAbled? 1
SYSTem:COMMunicate:LAN:APPLY
@wait 25
SYSTem:COMMunicate:LAN:CONnected?
SYSTem:COMMunicate:LAN:ADDRess?
SYSTem:COMMunicate:LAN:SAVE
